{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|trava}}, from {{inh|ca|la|trabs|trabem|t=beam, rafter}}. The ending may have been changed to /-a/ due to the word's feminine gender, or a new singular {{m|ca||trava}} could have been back-derived from the original plural {{m|ca||traves}} (cf. {{m|ca|xinxa}} < {{m|ca|xinxes}}). Alternately, {{m|ca||trava}} could simply be a deverbal of {{m|ca|travar}}, a verb derived from the same Latin source.

